From e3c17de06bce0ddc9de9fc560f7d3aa252a86047 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: stephan-xyz <stephan@zehrer.net>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 08:24:40 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] netstack: counters in /scheme/netcfg/stats

For diagnosis (redox-rpi #566, netdiag): frames read from and written to
the drivers and where they went (IPv4 for this host, ARP, another MAC,
malformed, another protocol), driver read and write errors, ARP
requests, expired entries and packets dropped waiting for ARP, the times
the router queues were full, packets without a route, the number of
sockets of each kind and of TCP sockets in each state (a socket that is
never freed shows as a growing count, REQ-NET-4), and one line per TCP
connection with its state and queue fill. The socket part is refreshed by
the main loop at most twice a second.
